{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"288ad50e4e6f4f6e2da56a7209ef618a357ed36fd9d6129651fd690d30b87583","digest":{"component_or_area":"LLM framework: provider seam, capability model, verdict provenance, and two-tier support policy","key_entities":["provider_factory hook","ProviderSession","ModelProfile","provider_provenance","capabilities.py","providers.py","model_classes.py","KNOWN_PROVIDER_NAMES","_REBAR_OVERRIDES","_MODEL_ID_CAPABILITY_OVERRIDES","BedrockModelProfile","first_class tier","best_effort tier","runner.py:405-407"],"problem_keywords":["ADR documentation","LLM provider seam","two-tier support policy","pydantic-ai provider factory","bedrock integration","provider registry","capability determination","verdict provenance stamping","prompt caching","model class configuration"],"propositions":["The provider seam is pydantic-ai's provider_factory hook; rebar builds a per-run SESSION object that returns a Provider, never shared or bare function, with client teardown via _closeables.","Capability decisions read ModelProfile field presence (native_structured_output, prompt_cache_style, supports_thinking, supports_temperature), NEVER provider-name strings; isinstance checks break stdlib-only import contract and CI.","Two-tier verdict provenance: first_class (Anthropic + Bedrock native builders, full fidelity, test + parity covered) vs best_effort (OpenAI-compatible intermediary, may rewrite, no JSON schema), both sign on every tier.","Registry membership by KNOWN_PROVIDER_NAMES literal (no imports, no lazy loading); guard order validates explicit provider FIRST before model-string inference; graceful fallback rejected; unrecognized inline prefix permitted.","Model classes (frontier/standard/trivial) are config SLOTS operator fills, not presets; three CALL SITES read them (not one funnel); cfg.model deprecated with migration window; per-step YAML declarations honored only in gates with model_ladder."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1786701123450287001,"uuid":"8e17fdaa-e8ee-441e-8cf3-591902067eb9"}